design-system:
# Design Style: Neo-Industrial Monochrome

Revision: 2 (synced with the implemented tools, 2026-11). Supersedes the earlier draft of this file.

## Scope and Source of Truth

This specification was extracted from a suite of production operator tools that run as Electron apps (plain HTML, CSS and vanilla JS, no UI framework) on a touchscreen tablet in a workshop / logistics environment:

- Launcher   -- home screen: app selection, system actions, Wi-Fi, brightness, help
- Deploy     -- flashing and provisioning devices (stepwise checklist + log + settings sidebar)
- Packing    -- scan-driven order packing (large status readouts + many confirmation dialogs)
- Return     -- processing returned devices (checklist + live customer info overlay)
- Stock      -- warehouse stock booking (tile grid + calculator dialogs)
- OTA update overlay -- full-screen system update progress screen

Where the tools differ from each other in small details, this file states ONE canonical value. The section "Known Deviations in the Reference Tools" lists what was normalized, so nobody copies an accident.

Token and class names marked "(canonical)" do not exist under that name in the reference code (the value is hard-coded or inline there). They are the names to use in a new project.

Out of scope -- do NOT treat as reference for this style: a dark-themed hardware diagnostics screen, a dark-themed USB stick flasher, and a legacy Bootstrap small-screen page that live in the same repository. They predate or deliberately ignore this system.

---

## Design Philosophy

### Core Principle

**Functional Brutalism.** Neo-Industrial Monochrome is designed for embedded, kiosk, and industrial operator interfaces where clarity and tactile feedback trump aesthetics. Every element is bold, high-contrast, and immediately readable. The UI communicates trust through consistency and physicality: components behave like real switches and buttons, pressing down when activated. This is design as engineering -- every visual choice has a functional justification.

### Visual Vibe

**Emotional Keywords**: Precise, Industrial, Tactile, Authoritative, Reliable, Operational, Functional, Urgent-ready, Confidence-inspiring, Unambiguous

This is the visual language of:
- Industrial HMI (Human-Machine Interface) panels
- Operator control terminals in logistics and manufacturing
- Embedded kiosk displays in warehouses and retail
- Swiss graphic design meets Bauhaus engineering
- Military / aerospace cockpit displays

The design commands immediate operator trust. Bold uppercase labels, mechanical-press button behavior, and stark black-on-white contrast mean a technician can read and interact at a glance, even under stress.

### What This Design Is NOT

- No soft, rounded, or "friendly consumer app" aesthetics
- No gradients as decoration, no decorative accent colors
- No blurred drop shadows, no "elevation" (Material Design style)
- No serif or editorial typography
- No animated or motion-heavy transitions
- Not a generic admin dashboard (Bootstrap gray, blue accents)
- Not touch-unfriendly (small tap targets, hover-only interactions)
- Not dark mode. The canvas is white. Black surfaces exist only as the log terminal and the screen-off overlay.

### The DNA of Neo-Industrial Monochrome

#### 1. High-Contrast Monochrome Structure
Pure black (#000000) and white (#FFFFFF) form the entire structural layer: page, cards, panels, borders, text. Off-white (#F9F9F9) is the resting surface of read-only readouts and utility controls. Light gray (#E5E5E5) is the face of a neutral button. There are no gray gradients and no soft neutrals in the structure.

#### 2. Solid Geometric "Press" Shadow
Buttons use a hard, offset, solid box-shadow (e.g. `4px 4px 0px #000000`) with zero blur. It is a 2D geometric offset that reads as physical depth. On press (:active) the shadow collapses to `0px 0px` and the element moves down-right with `transform: translate()` -- the button physically travels into its shadow.

The same hard shadow, without the press behavior, marks free-standing objects that float on the canvas (dialogs, corner badges, help cards, banners, toasts, tiles). Readouts embedded inside a card are flat.

#### 3. Sharp 90-Degree Geometry
Zero border-radius on every element, enforced globally with `!important`. One sanctioned exception exists: the circular status icon disc (see "Status Hero Screen").

#### 4. Uppercase Sans-Serif Typography
All headings, button labels, form labels and badges are UPPERCASE. Display type is Plus Jakarta Sans at weight 800. Body text is Inter. All technical data (ports, versions, IDs, serials, counters, percentages, logs, status readouts) is JetBrains Mono.

#### 5. Semantic Signal Colors
Color always carries machine or workflow state -- never decoration. Three status colors (teal OK, amber warning, red error) plus one action-signal yellow. They appear as text color, as the fill of small indicators, as the fill of semantic action buttons, as a thick accent bar, and as pale tints behind messages. They never color page structure. See "Semantic Color Rules".

#### 6. Touch-First Interactive Design
The UI assumes a touchscreen operated quickly, possibly with gloves. Primary-flow buttons are 48-80px tall. Hover styles exist only for desktop debugging and are wrapped in `@media (hover: hover)`.

#### 7. Mechanical Button Behavior (3-State Press)
1. Resting: offset shadow `4px 4px 0px #000`, shifted `translate(-2px, -2px)`, face #E5E5E5.
2. Hover (hover-capable devices only): shadow `2px 2px`, shift `translate(-1px, -1px)`, face inverts to #000000 with #FFFFFF text.
3. Active (press): shadow `0px 0px`, shift `translate(2px, 2px)`, face #222222 with #FFFFFF text.

This applies to every button, including colored ones: on hover and press they all become black. Color tells you what the button means at rest; black tells you it is being operated.

#### 8. Dashed = Auxiliary
A dashed black border marks an auxiliary, diagnostic or temporary zone (test panel, passive status notes, key-value dividers). Solid borders are for the real workflow.

---

## Design Token System

### Colors

```
/* Base Palette (structure) */
--bg:             #FFFFFF   Page and card background
--bg-color:       #FFFFFF   Alias of --bg (both names are in use)
--text-primary:   #000000   All primary text
--text-muted:     #525252   Secondary / helper text, field captions
--accent:         #000000   Black IS the accent
--border:         #000000   All structural borders
--border-light:   #E5E5E5   Subtle dividers, checklist row separators, slider track
--muted-bg:       #F9F9F9   Resting surface of readouts, utility buttons, section boxes
--btn-face:       #E5E5E5   (canonical) Neutral button face
--btn-pressed:    #222222   (canonical) Any button while pressed

/* Status Colors */
--status-ok:      #38B2AC   Teal  -- success, connected, done, positive confirm
--status-warn:    #FFD740   Amber -- in progress, attention, unsaved, active toggle, Help
--status-err:     #FF5252   Red   -- error, failure, destructive, exit/abort text

/* Action Signal */
--signal:         #FFE600   (canonical) Signal yellow -- the "do this next" action button,
                            toasts, freshly captured values. Brighter and greener than amber.

/* Message Tints (pale backgrounds behind status content) */
--tint-ok:        #E6FFFA   (canonical)
--tint-warn:      #FFF9E6   (canonical)
--tint-err:       #FFF5F5   (canonical)
--tint-info:      #E1F5FE   (canonical)

/* Terminal */
--term-bg:        #000000   (canonical) Log window background
--term-fg:        #FFFFFF   (canonical) Log text (phosphor green #00FF00 is the allowed alternative)

/* Overlays */
scrim:            rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4)        Behind dialogs
veil:             rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95) Blocking "please wait" overlay
```

Amber vs. signal yellow -- keep them apart:
- #FFD740 amber is a STATE color: something is running, pending, unsaved, selected, or needs attention.
- #FFE600 signal yellow is an ACTION color: the button the operator is expected to press next, or a transient highlight (toast, queue badge, "ID just read" chip).

### Typography

Font Stack:
- Display / Headings / Buttons / Labels: "Plus Jakarta Sans", sans-serif -- weight 800 (700 for checklist labels). Always UPPERCASE, letter-spacing 0.5-1px.
- Body / UI text: "Inter", -apple-system, sans-serif -- weight 400-600.
- Technical data: "JetBrains Mono", monospace -- weight 700-800.

Font loading (as in the reference):
```css
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@500;600;700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700;800&display=swap');
```
For an offline kiosk, self-host the same three families with @font-face instead; the system fallbacks (sans-serif / monospace) are not an acceptable permanent look.

Maximum weight is 800. Do not request 900 -- it is not loaded.

Type Scale (px values are used directly; the UI is a fixed-device app):
```
10px  - Field captions inside dense key-value grids, queue hints
11px  - Tags, step pills, sub-labels, tiny metadata, form labels in sidebars
12px  - Status badges, form labels, pills, small mono readouts
13px  - Utility button labels, compact body text, log text, badge text
14px  - Dialog body text, list items, secondary button labels, input text (Inter)
15px  - Standard button label, checklist label, mono input text, log readouts
16px  - Sidebar section heading, emphasized dialog text
18px  - Launcher button label, readout value (infofield), help card heading
20px  - Panel heading (h2), status headline, dialog heading (h4)
22px  - Alert / dialog heading (h3), big choice button title
24px  - Hero action button label, large dialog heading
26-28px - Blocking warning dialog heading
30-36px - "Please wait" overlay headline (36px canonical)
38px  - Single hero number (current stock) in JetBrains Mono
```

Tracking and Leading:
- Uppercase labels and buttons: letter-spacing 1px (buttons), 0.5px (headings, labels)
- System / standby text: letter-spacing 2px
- Body text: letter-spacing normal
- Line heights: 1.4-1.5 for UI and dialog text; 1.5 for logs; 1.7 for long-form markdown
- Text is not selectable (`user-select: none` on body). Only long-form documentation is selectable.

### Border Radius

```
ALL VALUES: 0px -- enforced via * { border-radius: 0px !important; }
```
The !important ensures no third-party stylesheet can reintroduce rounded corners. Sole exception: the status icon disc, which must opt out explicitly with an inline `border-radius: 50% !important`.

### Borders and Lines

```
hairline: 1px dashed #E5E5E5   Key-value row dividers
dashed:   1px dashed #000000   Divider inside a message box
light:    1px solid  #E5E5E5   Checklist row separators
tag:      1px solid  #000000   Tiny chips, inline code, test-result boxes
light+:   1.5px solid #000000  Compact items: tags, step pills, pills, table cells
thin:     2px solid  #000000   STANDARD: buttons, inputs, cards, readouts, panels
aux:      2px dashed #000000   Auxiliary / diagnostic / test zones
medium:   3px solid  #000000   Header underlines, message boxes inside dialogs, toasts
thick:    4px solid  #000000   Dialog outer border, blocking overlays
accent:   8px solid    Left accent bar of a status banner
```

Usage:
- Every interactive component has at minimum a 2px solid #000000 border.
- Panel and dialog headings carry `border-bottom: 2px solid` (sidebar, dialog) or `3px solid` (page-level header).
- Dialogs use `border: 4px solid`.
- Sections inside a sidebar are separated by an `hr` rendered as `border-top: 2px solid #000000`.

### Shadows

```
8px 8px 0px #000000    Dialogs
6px 6px 0px #000000    Toast, status header block, icon disc, hovered tile
4px 4px 0px #000000    Standard buttons, tiles, order cards, message boxes in dialogs
3px 3px 0px #000000    Corner status badges, help cards, banners, phase "active" pill
2px 2px 0px #000000    Utility buttons, keys, tabs, toggles, chips, data pills
1px 1px 0px #000000    Minimal elements (tags, device chips)

Button hover:   reduce by 50% (4px to 2px, 2px to 1px)
Button active:  collapse to 0px 0px 0px #000000
```

Rules:
- Blur is always 0. No `filter: drop-shadow`. No glow.
- Shadows are always #000000, always offset down-right, x equals y.
- The only blur permitted anywhere is `backdrop-filter: blur(4px)` on the dialog scrim.

Flat (no shadow):
- `.neu-card` panels that form the page layout -- depth comes from the border
- `.infofield`, `.inset-screen`, status readouts, checklists, inputs, selects
- `.badge` (static header readout)
- the keyboard container

### Spacing Scale

```
4 / 6 / 8 / 10 / 12 / 16 / 20 / 24 / 30 / 40 px

Outer page padding (tool screens):   10px
Gap between layout columns/panels:   12px
Panel (card) padding:                20px
Launcher card padding:               40px
Dialog padding:                      24px standard, 30px for alerts / confirmations
Compact card padding:                14-16px
Gap between dialog buttons:          12-16px
Gap between launcher buttons:        20px
Gap between corner buttons:          12px
Gap between stacked badges:          8px
Gap inside chip rows:                6px
Corner offset from screen edge:      20px
Checklist row padding:               10px 18px
```

### Z-Index Layers

```
1         Main content
10        Fixed corner widgets (status, devices)
100       Fixed corner controls (buttons, brightness)
500       Environment banner (test mode)
1000      Dialogs. A dialog opened from another dialog takes +10 (1010, 1020, ...)
1050      Alert dialog -- always above all other dialogs
2000      Full-screen modal (Help)
9990      Brightness dim overlay
10000     Blocking "please wait" overlay
10050     Toast
99999     Fullscreen log (close button +1)
999999    Screen-off overlay (topmost)
```

---

## Foundation Stylesheet

Port this block first. It is the consolidated common base of all reference tools. Everything in "Component Stylings" builds on it.

```css
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@500;600;700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700;800&display=swap');

:root {
  --bg: #FFFFFF;
  --bg-color: #FFFFFF;
  --text-primary: #000000;
  --text-muted: #525252;
  --accent: #000000;
  --border: #000000;
  --border-light: #E5E5E5;
  --muted-bg: #F9F9F9;
  --btn-face: #E5E5E5;
  --btn-pressed: #222222;

  --status-ok: #38B2AC;
  --status-warn: #FFD740;
  --status-err: #FF5252;
  --signal: #FFE600;

  --tint-ok: #E6FFFA;
  --tint-warn: #FFF9E6;
  --tint-err: #FFF5F5;
  --tint-info: #E1F5FE;

  --font-display: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif;
  --font-body: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
}

* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border-radius: 0px !important; /* non-negotiable */
}

body {
  width: 100vw;
  height: 100vh;
  overflow: hidden;              /* kiosk: the page never scrolls */
  background-color: #FFFFFF;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  user-select: none;
}

h1, h2, h3, h4 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  color: var(--text-primary);
}

/* ---------- Panel ---------- */
.neu-card {
  background-color: var(--bg);
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  padding: 20px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  box-shadow: none;
  min-width: 0;
}

/* ---------- Button ---------- */
button,
.btn-neu {
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  outline: none;
  background-color: var(--btn-face);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: 15px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 1px;
  height: 54px;
  cursor: pointer;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  transition: all 0.1s ease-out;
  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #000000;
  transform: translate(-2px, -2px);
}

/* !important is intentional: hover and press must win over every color variant */
@media (hover: hover) {
  button:not(:disabled):hover,
  .btn-neu:not(:disabled):hover {
    background-color: var(--text-primary) !important;
    color: #FFFFFF !important;
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000000 !important;
    transform: translate(-1px, -1px) !important;
  }
}

button:not(:disabled):active,
.btn-neu:not(:disabled):active {
  background-color: var(--btn-pressed) !important;
  color: #FFFFFF !important;
  box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px #000000 !important;
  transform: translate(2px, 2px) !important;
}

button:disabled,
.btn-neu:disabled {
  opacity: 0.5;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

button:focus-visible,
select:focus-visible,
input:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid var(--border);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* ---------- Form ---------- */
.neu-input,
.neu-select {
  width: 100%;
  height: 48px;
  padding: 0 12px;
  background-color: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 15px;
  outline: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}

.neu-input:focus,
.neu-select:focus {
  border-width: 3px;
  background-color: var(--muted-bg);
}

/* ---------- Dialog ---------- */
.modal-overlay {
  display: none;                 /* shown by setting display: flex */
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 1000;
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}

.modal-content {
  background-color: var(--bg);
  border: 4px solid var(--border);
  padding: 24px;
  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0px #000000;
  max-width: 500px;
  width: 90%;
}

/* ---------- Spinner ---------- */
.spinner {
  width: 50px;
  height: 50px;
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  margin: 0 auto 30px auto;
  position: relative;
  animation: spin 3s linear infinite;
}
.spinner::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 10px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-light);
}
.spinner::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 50%;
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  background-color: var(--text-primary);
  transform: translateX(-50%);
}
@keyframes spin { 100% { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
```

---

## Component Stylings

### Buttons -- Sizes

All sizes share the foundation button. Only dimensions and font size change.

| Role | Class | Size | Font | Shadow / rest shift |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Launcher app button | `.btn-neu` + (canonical) `.btn-xl` | 200 x 70px | 18px | 4px / -2px |
| Hero action (START ...) | (canonical) `.btn-hero` | 100% x 80px | 24px | 4px / -2px |
| Standard | `.btn-neu` | auto x 54px | 15px | 4px / -2px |
| Dialog action | `.btn-neu` | flex x 48-60px | 14-18px | 4px / -2px |
| Sidebar / system | `.btn-sys` | 100% x 48px | 14px | 4px / -2px |
| Inline next to input | `.btn-small` | auto x 48px, padding 0 16px | 13px | 4px / -2px |
| Corner utility | (canonical) `.btn-util` | 130px or auto x 40px, padding 0 16px | 13px | 2px / -1px |
| Dense inline (secondary only) | -- | auto x 32-36px, padding 0 12px | 11-12px | 2px / -1px |

In a row of dialog buttons, give each `flex: 1` so they share the width; the affirmative button may take `flex: 2`.

Utility buttons (2px shadow tier) use a shorter travel:
```css
/* Resting */
height: 40px; font-size: 13px; padding: 0 16px;
background-color: #F9F9F9;
box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000000;
transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
/* Hover */   box-shadow: 1px 1px 0px #000000; transform: translate(0px, 0px);  background #000, color #FFF
/* Active */  box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px #000000; transform: translate(1px, 1px);  background #222, color #FFF
```

### Buttons -- Meaning (Face Color)

The face color at rest tells the operator what the button does. Hover and press always turn it black.

| Variant | Class | Rest face / text | Use for |
|---|---|---|---|
| Neutral | `.btn-neu` | #E5E5E5 / #000 | Cancel, close, back, secondary actions |
| Primary | `.btn-neu-primary` | #FFFFFF / #000 | The main action of a panel or dialog in a calm context (Start, Apply, Retry, OK). White stands out against the gray neutral buttons. |
| Option | `.btn-neu-primary` | #FFFFFF / #000 | One of several equal choices (pick a color, pick a model) |
| Signal | (canonical) `.btn-neu-signal` | #FFE600 / #000 | The one action the workflow is waiting for: proceed, confirm packed, retry, print |
| Confirm | `.btn-neu-ready` | #38B2AC / #FFFFFF | Positive commit: yes-book-it, save, understood, refresh data |
| Danger | (canonical) `.btn-neu-danger` | #FF5252 / #FFFFFF | Destructive commit: delete, overwrite |
| Danger text | (canonical) `.btn-neu-danger-text` | #E5E5E5 or #FFFFFF / #FF5252 | Leave or abort: EXIT, BACK, SKIP, ABORT, RESET. Low-emphasis but unmistakable. |
| Attention | -- | #FFD740 / #000 | Help button; reopen-info button. At most one per screen. |

Rules:
- Per dialog: at most one Signal, Confirm or Danger button. Everything else is Neutral or Danger text.
- The affirmative button sits on the LEFT in two-button confirmation rows (YES | CANCEL) in the stock/packing dialogs, and on the RIGHT in system warning dialogs (Skip | Retry). Pick one convention per project; the right-aligned variant (`justify-content: flex-end`) is canonical for compact alerts.
- Disabled: `opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed;` and no hover/press reaction. A button that is waiting for a background process is disabled AND its label says why.
- State feedback on a neutral button (e.g. "Hotspot" on/off) is given by text color only: teal when on, red when off.

### Button -- Help / Attention (#btnOpenHelp)

```css
/* Resting */
height: 40px; padding: 0 16px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.5px; gap: 6px;
background-color: #FFD740;
color: #000000;
border: 2px solid #000000;
box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000000;
transform: translate(-1px, -1px);

/* Hover */   background-color: #000000; color: #FFD740; box-shadow: 1px 1px 0px #000; transform: translate(0, 0);
/* Active */  background-color: #222222; color: #FFD740; box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px #000; transform: translate(1px, 1px);
```
Note the inversion keeps amber as the text color.

### Icon Button (dialog close, password reveal)

Small square button embedded in a header or input. It does not use the press shadow.
```css
width: 32px; height: 32px; padding: 0;
font-size: 16px;
background: #F9F9F9;
border: 1px solid #000000;
box-shadow: none; transform: none;
```
Glyph: multiplication X (U+2715) for close.

### Big Choice Button (.initial-device-btn)

Two-line button for a first-run or branching choice.
```css
height: 110px; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding: 16px; background-color: #FFFFFF;

.initial-device-title { font: 800 22px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.initial-device-sub   { font: 700 13px 'JetBrains Mono'; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid currentColor; text-transform: uppercase; }
```
Lay out choices in `display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px;`. `currentColor` makes the sub-chip border invert together with the text on hover.

### Cards / Panels (.neu-card)

```css
background-color: #FFFFFF;
border: 2px solid #000000;
padding: 20px;          /* 40px on the launcher */
box-shadow: none;       /* layout panels are flat */
```

Panel heading patterns:
```css
/* Main panel: title row with badges on the right */
h2 { font-size: 20px; }                       /* row: display flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 15px */

/* Sidebar section */
h2 { font-size: 16px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-bottom: 12px; }

/* Page-level heading inside a large panel */
h2 { font-size: 22px; border-bottom: 3px solid #000; padding-bottom: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
```

Compact card (floating info card, e.g. inside Help):
```css
background: #FFFFFF; border: 2px solid #000000; padding: 14px;
box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px #000000;
display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;
```
Compact card header: `font: 800 14px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; border-bottom: 2px solid #E5E5E5; padding-bottom: 6px; display: flex; gap: 6px;`

Hero info card (.compact-hero-card): same, but `background: #F9F9F9; padding: 16px;` with title (18px) + muted description (13px, weight 500) on the left and a tag stack on the right.

Section box (grouping inside a dialog or overlay):
```css
border: 2px solid #000000; background: #F9F9F9; padding: 12px 14px;
display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;
```
Section title: `font: 800 12px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.6px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; padding-bottom: 5px;`

### Read-Only Readouts

Info field (.infofield) -- one-line status readout:
```css
font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
font-weight: 800;
font-size: 18px;            /* 15px inside dense tool panels */
padding: 12px 24px;         /* 10px 16px dense */
background: #F9F9F9;
border: 2px solid #000000;
box-shadow: none;
text-align: center;
width: 100%;                /* or inline-block with min-width: 300px on the launcher */
```
A left-aligned 52px-high variant (flex, `padding: 0 20px`) sits directly under the hero action button.

Status headline (.status-indicator) -- names the current workflow step:
```css
font: 800 20px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;
padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 15px;
background: #F9F9F9; border: 2px solid #000000; text-align: center;
```
Its text color follows state: black (neutral), --status-ok (success), --status-err (error).

Inset screen (.inset-screen) -- multi-line data display:
```css
flex: 1; min-height: 0; min-width: 0;
background: #FFFFFF; color: #000000;
border: 2px solid #000000;
padding: 16px;
font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5;
white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-y: auto;
```
Two inset screens side by side (`display: flex; gap: 12px`) form the main readout of a scan-driven screen.

Hero number -- one big value in a box:
```css
/* box */    border: 3px solid #000; padding: 12px; background: #F9F9F9; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #000; text-align: center;
/* caption */ font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; color: #525252;
/* value */   font: 800 38px 'JetBrains Mono'; line-height: 1;
```

### Badges, Tags, Pills, Chips

All are JetBrains Mono, uppercase, non-interactive.

| Element | Class | Spec |
|---|---|---|
| Header badge | `.badge` | 13px / 700, padding 4px 10px, border 1px solid #000, background #F9F9F9, no shadow |
| Corner status badge | -- | 12px / 700, padding 8px 14px, border 2px, background #F9F9F9, shadow 3px 3px |
| Tag | `.compact-tag` | 11px / 700, padding 3px 8px, border 1.5px, background #FFFFFF, shadow 1px 1px |
| Status pill | `.clickup-pill` + modifier | 11px / 800, padding 2px 7px, border 1.5px, no shadow |
| Data chip | -- | 12px / bold, padding 4px 10px, border 2px, background #FFFFFF, shadow 2px 2px |
| Count chip on a tile | `.pos-card-stock` | 12px / 700, padding 2px 8px, border 2px, background #FFF9E6, shadow 2px 2px |
| Value highlight | -- | 12px / bold, padding 2px 6px, border 2px, background #FFE600, shadow 2px 2px |
| Mode badge (amber) | `.help-badge` | 12px / 800, padding 2px 8px, border 2px, background #FFD740, shadow 2px 2px |
| Priority badge | `.prio-badge` | sans 11px / 800, padding 3px 8px, letter-spacing 1px, background #FF5252, color #FFF, no border |

Status pill modifiers:
```css
.clickup-pill-ok      { background: #38B2AC; color: #FFFFFF; }
.clickup-pill-warn    { background: #FFD740; color: #000000; }
.clickup-pill-err     { background: #FF5252; color: #FFFFFF; }
.clickup-pill-neutral { background: #FFFFFF; color: #000000; }
```

Meta tags in dense lists (order age, item count, IDs): `font-size: 11px; font-weight: 800; padding: 2px 7px; border: 1px solid;` on a tint background (--tint-ok, --tint-warn, --tint-info, or #F9F9F9 for neutral). They sit in a `display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px` row.

### Status LED (.status-led)

A square indicator -- never a circle. Four states, each with color AND glyph so it works without color vision.

```css
.status-led {
  width: 22px; height: 22px;
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  margin-right: 15px;
  background-color: var(--bg);
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 800;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  transition: all 0.1s ease;
}

/* 0: waiting / inactive */
.status-led.state-0 { background-color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--border-light); }

/* 1: error */
.status-led.state-1 { background-color: var(--status-err); color: #FFFFFF; }
.status-led.state-1::after { content: "\2717"; }      /* ballot X */

/* 2: processing -- amber with moving diagonal stripes */
.status-led.state-2 {
  background-color: var(--status-warn); color: #000000;
  background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, transparent, transparent 3px, rgba(0,0,0,0.15) 3px, rgba(0,0,0,0.15) 6px);
  background-size: 24px 24px;
  animation: progress-stripe 1.2s linear infinite;
}
.status-led.state-2::after { content: "\2026"; }      /* ellipsis */

/* 3: done */
.status-led.state-3 { background-color: var(--status-ok); color: #FFFFFF; }
.status-led.state-3::after { content: "\2713"; }      /* check mark */

@keyframes progress-stripe {
  0%   { background-position: 0 0; }
  100% { background-position: 24px 0; }
}
```
A 12px variant without glyph is used as an inline activity dot.

### Checklist (.worker-checklist)

The standard way to show a multi-step process.

```css
.worker-checklist { display: flex; flex-direction: column; background: #FFFFFF; border: 2px solid #000; padding: 4px 0; }
.check-row        { display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 10px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid #E5E5E5; }
.check-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.check-label      { font: 700 15px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
```
Row anatomy: `[status-led] [label] [optional inline extras]`. Extras that may follow the label in the same row: an inline progress bar + percentage, a row of test-result boxes, a freshly read value highlight, or a small retry button pushed right with `margin-left: auto`.

Test-result box (per-component pass/fail inside a row):
```css
/* box */   width: 18px; height: 18px; border: 1px solid #000; color: #FFF; font: bold 11px 'JetBrains Mono';
            background: var(--status-ok) | var(--status-err) | #888888 (not applicable);
            content: check U+2713 | ballot X U+2717 | hyphen
/* label */ font: bold 12px 'JetBrains Mono'; text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 6px;
```

### Step Pills (horizontal process strip)

Compact alternative to the checklist, for a process running in the background.
```css
.clickup-step-pills { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(8, 1fr); gap: 6px; }   /* one column per step */
.clickup-step-pill  { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 5px; padding: 4px;
                      border: 1.5px solid #000; background: #F9F9F9;
                      font: 700 11px 'JetBrains Mono'; text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }
.step-running { background: #FFD740; color: #000; animation: pulse 1s infinite alternate; }
.step-ok      { background: #38B2AC; color: #FFF; }
.step-fail    { background: #FF5252; color: #FFF; }

@keyframes pulse { 0% { opacity: 0.4; } 100% { opacity: 1; } }
```
Label format: number + short noun ("1 USB", "2 ID", "7 FLASH").

Phase steps (3 large steps, used on the update screen): 2px border, white, mono 12px/700 uppercase, `padding: 8px 10px`, leading glyph white circle U+25CB (pending) / black circle U+25CF (active) / check U+2713 (done). `done` = background #E6FFFA; `active` = background #FFD740, weight 800, shadow 3px 3px.

### Progress Bar

Inline (inside a checklist row):
```css
/* track */ height: 16px; flex-grow: 1; background: #F9F9F9; border: 2px solid #000; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: none;
/* fill */  height: 100%; background: var(--status-ok); transition: width 0.1s ease;
/* text */  font: 800 13px 'JetBrains Mono'; min-width: 40px; text-align: right; margin-left: 10px;
```

Hero (dedicated progress screen):
```css
/* track */ height: 26-36px; background: #FFFFFF; border: 3px solid #000; overflow: hidden;
/* fill */  background: var(--status-ok); border-right: 3px solid #000; transition: width 0.45s ease-out;
/* indeterminate */ width: 100%; border-right: none;
   background: repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, #FFD740, #FFD740 16px, #FFF3B0 16px, #FFF3B0 32px);
   background-size: 45px 45px; animation: moveStripes 1.1s linear infinite;
/* finishing */     same stripes in #38B2AC / #81E6D9
/* retrying */      solid #FF5252

@keyframes moveStripes { 0% { background-position: 0 0; } 100% { background-position: 45px 0; } }
```
Diagonal moving stripes are the system`s universal "working" texture (LED state 2, indeterminate progress). The percentage is shown beside the bar in JetBrains Mono 800, 20-30px on a hero screen.

Countdown bar (auto-dismiss): 6px track, 1px border, fill shrinking linearly from 100% to 0.

### Inputs / Selects (.neu-input, .neu-select)

```css
height: 48px; padding: 0 12px;
border: 2px solid #000000; background: #FFFFFF;
font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px;   /* technical values */
outline: none; box-shadow: none;

/* Focus */
border-width: 3px;
background-color: #F9F9F9;
```
- Fields holding natural-language text may use Inter 600 / 14px instead.
- Read-only field: background #F0F0F0. Disabled field: background #E9ECEF, color #495057.
- Keyboard focus (focus-visible) adds `outline: 3px solid #000; outline-offset: 2px`. No colored focus rings, ever.

Form label:
```css
display: block; margin-bottom: 6px;
font: 800 12px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; text-transform: uppercase; color: #000000;
```
Two fields side by side: `display: flex; gap: 12px;` each `flex: 1`. Input + action: `display: flex; gap: 10px;` with a `.btn-small` of the same 48px height.

### Checkbox (.form-check-neu)

```css
.form-check-neu { display: flex; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px; cursor: pointer; }
.form-check-neu span { font: 700 14px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }

.form-check-neu input[type="checkbox"] {
  appearance: none;
  width: 28px; height: 28px;
  background-color: #FFFFFF;
  border: 2px solid #000000;
  margin-right: 12px;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  cursor: pointer; outline: none;
}
.form-check-neu input[type="checkbox"]:checked { background-color: #000000; }
.form-check-neu input[type="checkbox"]:checked::after {
  content: "\2713"; color: #FFFFFF;
  font: 800 18px 'JetBrains Mono';
}
```
The whole label row is the tap target. Checked = solid black square with a white check.

### Range / Slider

```css
/* Track */
-webkit-appearance: none; appearance: none;
width: 120px; height: 6px;
background: #E5E5E5; border: 1px solid #000000;

/* Thumb (both ::-webkit-slider-thumb and ::-moz-range-thumb) */
-webkit-appearance: none;
width: 14px; height: 18px;
background: #000000; border: 1px solid #000000;
```
The thumb is a flat black rectangular block. The slider lives inside a bar container: `height: 40px; padding: 0 16px; gap: 12px; background: #F9F9F9; border: 2px solid #000; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000;` with an uppercase 12px/800 caption on the left and the value in JetBrains Mono 12px/800 (`min-width: 42px`) on the right.

### Keyboard Keys (.key)

On-screen keyboard for text entry in kiosk context.

```css
.key {
  height: 42px; flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 32px; padding: 0;
  background: #FFFFFF;
  border: 2px solid #000000;
  box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000000;
  transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-weight: bold; font-size: 15px;
  text-transform: none;            /* keys show their real case */
}
.key:active       { box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px #000; transform: translate(1px, 1px); background: #E5E5E5; }
.key.active-shift { background: #000000; color: #FFFFFF; }
```
Container: `background: #F9F9F9; padding: 8px; border: 2px solid #000; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px;` (no shadow). Each row: `display: flex; gap: 6px; justify-content: center;`. Wide keys use `flex-grow`: Shift and Backspace 1.5, Space 8. Row order: digits + backspace, three letter rows, one symbol row, space bar. Use the local keyboard layout of the operators.

### Dialogs

Scrim:
```css
position: fixed; inset: 0;
background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
z-index: 1000;
```

Dialog card:
```css
background: #FFFFFF;
border: 4px solid #000000;
box-shadow: 8px 8px 0px #000000;
padding: 24px;                     /* 30px for alerts and confirmations */
width: 90%; max-width: 500px;      /* 400 choice, 500 alert, 600 warning, 800 list, 1020 info overlay */
max-height: 90vh;
```

Anatomy, top to bottom:
1. Heading -- h3/h4, 20-22px (26-28px for blocking warnings), optional warning-sign emoji prefix. Colored --status-err when the dialog reports a problem; black otherwise. Optional `border-bottom: 2px solid #000; padding-bottom: 6-10px`.
2. Body text -- Inter 14-16px, weight 500, line-height 1.5, color #000 (or #525252 for calm explanations with the key terms in bold black).
3. Optional message box (see below) carrying the concrete data: serial, item name, before/after values.
4. Button row -- `display: flex; gap: 12-16px; margin-top: 20px;`, buttons 48-60px tall.

Alignment: alerts are left-aligned text with a right-aligned OK button. Confirmations and warnings are center-aligned with full-width button rows.

Message box (inside a dialog):
```css
border: 3px solid #000000;
padding: 15-20px;
box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #000000;      /* optional; omit in dense dialogs */
font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.5-1.6;
background: var(--tint-warn)  -- caution / already-done / check this
            var(--tint-err)   -- error / destructive target
            var(--tint-ok)    -- positive notice
            var(--tint-info)  -- neutral instruction
            #F9F9F9           -- plain data
```
Inside it: the critical identifier in JetBrains Mono 18-22px/800 colored --status-err on its own line, separated by `border-top: 1px dashed #000; padding-top: 5px`. A quantity is shown as an inverted block: `background: #000; color: #FFF; padding: 2px 12px; font-size: 22px`.

Before -> after preview (stock change, calculators): a message box with three columns `[CURRENT] arrow [CHANGE] = [NEW]`; captions 10px bold uppercase muted, values JetBrains Mono 18-22px; the change in orange-red #E65100 or --status-err/--status-ok by sign, the result in --status-ok.

Quick-adjust button grid: `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 12px;` buttons 46px, 16px; negative steps on --tint-err with red text, positive steps on --tint-ok with teal text.

Large info overlay (dialog with fixed header/footer): card `padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden; max-width: 1020px; width: 95vw; max-height: 92vh`.
- Header: `padding: 12px 20px; background: #F9F9F9; border-bottom: 3px solid #000;` title 18px + pills, minimize button on the right.
- Optional live strip: `padding: 10px 20px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000;` with activity LED, status text, step pills.
- Body: `flex: 1; overflow-y: auto; padding: 16px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;`
- Footer: `padding: 12px 20px; background: #F9F9F9; border-top: 3px solid #000; display: flex; gap: 14px;`

Stacking: a dialog opened from a dialog gets a higher z-index (+10). The alert dialog is always on top.

### Status Banner (.clickup-banner)

Message block with a thick status bar on the left.
```css
border: 2px solid #000000;
padding: 10px 14px;
box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px #000000;

.banner-loading { background: #F9F9F9; }
.banner-ok      { background: #E6FFFA; border-left: 8px solid var(--status-ok); }
.banner-warn    { background: #FFF9E6; border-left: 8px solid var(--status-warn); }
.banner-err     { background: #FFF5F5; border-left: 8px solid var(--status-err); }
```
Title: Plus Jakarta Sans 15px uppercase bold with an emoji prefix; text 13px/600, line-height 1.4. Text stays black on all variants.

Flat callout (note, warning footer): `border: 2-3px solid #000; background: var(--tint-warn); padding: 10px 14px;` with an 11px/800 uppercase caption line.

### Key-Value Displays

List form (.compact-kv-list):
```css
.compact-kv-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 1px dashed #E5E5E5; padding-bottom: 4px; }
.compact-kv-key { font-weight: 700; font-size: 12px; }
.compact-kv-val { font: 700 12px 'JetBrains Mono'; color: #38B2AC; }
```

Grid form (.clickup-kv-grid) -- caption above value:
```css
display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px 12px; font-size: 13px;
.clickup-kv-label { display: block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px; color: #525252; margin-bottom: 2px; }
.clickup-kv-val   { font-weight: 700; color: #000; word-break: break-word; line-height: 1.3; }
.clickup-kv-full  { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
```

Telemetry box (one boxed value): `border: 2px solid #000; background: #FFF; padding: 10px 14px;` key Plus Jakarta Sans 11px/800 uppercase muted, value JetBrains Mono 12-15px/800 with ellipsis overflow. Arrange in `grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 12px`.

### Tiles (.pos-card)

Square, pressable catalogue tile with picture, name and a count chip.
```css
.pos-card {
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  border: 2px solid #000; background: #FFF; padding: 12px;
  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #000;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
  cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.1s ease-out;
}
@media (hover: hover) {
  .pos-card:hover { transform: translate(-2px, -2px); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #000; background: #F9F9F9; }
}
.pos-card:active { transform: translate(2px, 2px); box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px #000; }

.pos-card-img   { width: 100%; flex-grow: 1; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid #000; background: #FFF; margin-bottom: 8px; }  /* img: object-fit: contain */
.pos-card-title { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; text-align: center; line-height: 1.25; height: 28px; }  /* 2-line clamp */
```
Tiles rest flat on the grid and LIFT on hover (the opposite of buttons, which start lifted) -- they are objects to pick up, not switches. Grid: `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(160px, 1fr)); gap: 15px; overflow-y: auto;`.

Category header inside the grid: `grid-column: 1 / -1; border-bottom: 3px double #000; padding-bottom: 5px;` with a 14px/800 uppercase label carrying `border-left: 5px solid #FFE600; padding-left: 8px`.

Missing picture: a 48px square line icon (stroke 2, square caps, miter joins) in #A0A0A0.

### List Cards (.order-card-item)

Row card in a scrollable work list.
```css
border: 2px solid #000; background: #FFF; padding: 14px;
display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px;
box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #000;

.is-prio { border: 3px solid #FF5252; background: #FFF5F5; }
```
Left: a wrap row of badges/meta tags (gap 6px) above the main line (16px/800, line-height 1.35). Right: a fixed 170px column with one Signal button (48px). List container: `display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; overflow-y: auto; padding: 4px;` (the padding keeps shadows from being clipped).

### Selection States

Three idioms -- choose by what the control is:

1. Tab (.help-tab) -- exclusive navigation. Active = pressed in and inverted.
```css
/* default */ height: 44px; flex: 1 1 auto; padding: 0 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; gap: 6px; white-space: nowrap;
              background: #F9F9F9; border: 2px solid #000; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000; transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
/* .active */ background: #000; color: #FFF; box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px #000; transform: translate(1px, 1px);
```
Tab bar: `display: flex; gap: 8px; overflow-x: auto; padding-bottom: 6px; scrollbar-width: thin;`

2. Toggle (.btn-help-subtle) -- a mode that is on or off. Active = pressed in and amber.
```css
/* default */ height: 44px; padding: 0 16px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; background: #FFF;
              border: 2px solid #000; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000; transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
/* .active */ background: #FFD740; color: #000; font-weight: 800; box-shadow: 0px 0px 0px #000; transform: translate(1px, 1px);
/* hover */   background: #FFF9C4;
```

3. Swatch filter -- a button whose face IS a data color (so it cannot change face to show selection). Active = raised with a ring.
```css
.active { border: 3px solid #000; outline: 3px solid #00E676; outline-offset: 1px;
          box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #000; transform: translateY(-2px); font-weight: 800; z-index: 2; }
```

Unsaved-changes state (.settings-dirty): the container of the changed settings gets `background-color: #FFD740; border: 2px solid #000;` (reserve the space with a transparent 2px border and `padding: 8px 10px 10px; margin: 0 -10px 10px;` so nothing shifts) and its save button turns white. Transition `0.15s ease` on background and border color.

### Log Panel

A collapsible terminal at the bottom of the work column or sidebar.

```css
.log-panel          { height: 52px; padding: 12px 18px; overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-shrink: 0; transition: height 0.2s ease; }
.log-panel.expanded { flex: 1; height: auto; min-height: 150px; }

/* header row: 22px high, space-between, cursor pointer */
/* label */         font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;   ("SYSTEM LOGS ...")
.log-toggle-icon    { width: 24px; height: 24px; font: 800 14px 'JetBrains Mono'; transform: rotate(180deg); transition: transform 0.2s ease; }
.log-panel.expanded .log-toggle-icon { transform: rotate(0deg); }     /* glyph: black up-pointing triangle U+25B2 */

#consoleDataLog {
  width: 100%; height: 100%; margin-top: 12px;
  background-color: #000000; color: #FFFFFF;
  border: 2px solid #000000; padding: 12px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5;
  white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; overflow-y: auto;
  opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.1s ease;
}
.log-panel.expanded #consoleDataLog { opacity: 1; }

/* scrollbar */  width: 12px; track #111111; thumb #444444 with 2px #111111 border
```
Tapping the log opens it fullscreen: `position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 99999; border: 4px solid #000; padding: 30px;`, with a close button fixed top-right (48 x 48px, black face, white glyph heavy X U+2716, inverts on hover, z-index +1).

An optional metadata strip above the log: `border: 1px solid #000; background: #F9F9F9; padding: 12px; font: 13px 'JetBrains Mono';` with bold keys.

### Blocking "Please Wait" Overlay (#update-window)

```css
display: none;  /* flex when active */
position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 10000;
background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
border: 4px solid #000000;
flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center;

.update-text    { font: 800 36px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; }
.update-subtext { font-size: 18px; color: #525252; margin-top: 10px; }
```
Content order: spinner, headline, sub-line. When a queue is being processed, a signal-yellow badge (mono 15px/800 uppercase, 3px border, 4px shadow) sits between spinner and headline, and upcoming items are listed below as data chips.

### Spinner

A rotating concentric-square construct -- never a circular spinner.
```
outer square: 50 x 50px, border 2px solid #000, animation spin 3s linear infinite
inner square (::before): inset 10px, border 1px solid #E5E5E5
marker (::after): 10 x 10px black square, top edge, horizontally centered
```
A 40px version is used inline in lists; a 46-62px version with 3px border on the update screen.

### Toast

```css
position: fixed; top: 25px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 10050;
background: #FFE600; color: #000000;
border: 3px solid #000000;
box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #000000;
padding: 12px 25px;
font: 800 15px 'JetBrains Mono'; text-transform: uppercase;
pointer-events: none;
transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
```
For transient, non-blocking notices only (e.g. duplicate scan ignored). Anything that needs a decision is a dialog.

### Environment Banner and Test Panel

Banner (test / simulation mode active):
```css
position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; z-index: 500;
background-color: #FFD740; color: #000000;
border-bottom: 2px solid #000000;
padding: 8px 16px; text-align: center;
font: 800 13px 'Plus Jakarta Sans'; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
```
Body gets `padding-top: 40px` while it is visible.

Test / diagnostic panel: `border: 2px dashed #000; background: #FFF; padding: 20px;` with a 15px heading. Its sub-sections are separated by `border-top: 2px dashed #000`. Passive status notes use the same dashed border on #F9F9F9 with JetBrains Mono 13px.

### Status Hero Screen

Large state message rendered inside the main readout area when the workflow reaches a decisive state (done, blocked, error).

```css
/* layout */ display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; height: 100%; padding: 25px; text-align: center;

/* status header block */
border: 3px solid #000; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #000; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px; width: 100%;
background: #FFD740 (action required, black text) | #FF5252 (error, white text);
h2 { font-size: 24-26px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0; }

/* body box */
border: 3px solid #000; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #000; padding: 20px; background: #FFF;
font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.5;

/* status icon disc -- the ONLY round element in the system */
width: 100px; height: 100px; border-radius: 50% !important;
border: 4px solid #000; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #000;
background: #FF5252 | #FFD740;
/* glyph 55-60px, white on red, black on amber */

/* headline under the disc */  font-size: 30px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; color matches the disc
/* divider */                  border-top: 2px solid #000; width: 80%;
```

### Launcher Corner Widgets

Status badge stack (bottom-left): `display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; align-items: flex-start;` of corner status badges. The status text color follows state (muted / teal / red).

Device widget (bottom-right): container mono 11px/700 uppercase, `padding: 6px 10px; border: 2px solid #000; background: #F9F9F9; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px #000; max-width: 480px; text-align: right;` -- a caption line with a count, then a right-aligned wrap row of device chips:
```css
padding: 3px 6px; font-size: 11px; text-transform: none;
border: 1px solid #000; box-shadow: 1px 1px 0px #000;
background: var(--tint-ok) (ready) | var(--tint-info) (present) | var(--tint-err) (fault);
```

Wi-Fi list item (.wifi-item):
```css
padding: 10px 15px; border-bottom: 2px solid #E5E5E5;
display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;
font: bold 14px 'JetBrains Mono'; cursor: pointer; transition: background 0.1s ease;
/* hover */ background: #F9F9F9;
```
The list sits in a `border: 2px solid #000; height: 200px; overflow-y: auto` box. An inline status line above it is a readout box whose border color and 10%-alpha background switch to the status color on success / error.

### Full-Screen Modal (Help)

The help system replaces the whole viewport -- it is not a floating dialog.
```css
/* overlay */ position: fixed; inset: 0; background: #FFFFFF; z-index: 2000;
/* content */ width: 100vw; height: 100vh; padding: 16px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; border: none; box-shadow: none; overflow: hidden;
```
- Header: `display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; border-bottom: 3px solid #000; padding-bottom: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px;` -- title (20px/800 uppercase, 24px emoji, amber mode badge), search input (38px high, Inter 13px/600, 2px border, max-width 360px), toggle button, close button.
- Close button: 44px, #E5E5E5, 2px shadow; its hover face is --status-err with white text (the only button whose hover is not black).
- Tab bar (see Selection States).
- Body: `flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto; padding: 4px;` -- hero card, then `display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 14px;` of compact cards.

Step list item: `display: flex; gap: 10px; background: #F9F9F9; border: 1.5px solid #000; padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 13px;` with a 22 x 22px black number badge (white JetBrains Mono 12px/800), a bold 13px title and a muted 12px/500 description.

FAQ item: `background: #FFF9E6; border: 1.5px solid #000; padding: 10px; font-size: 12px;` question 800 black, answer 500 muted, line-height 1.4. Error variant: `background: #FFF5F5; border-color: #FF5252`. A search hit is marked with `border: 2px solid #FFD740`.

### Markdown / Long-Form Viewer (.markdown-body)

```css
font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: #111111;
padding: 24px 32px; background: #FFF; border: 2px solid #000; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000;
max-width: 1350px; margin: 0 auto 30px; user-select: text;

h1 { font-size: 22px; border-bottom: 3px solid #000; padding-bottom: 8px; margin: 18px 0 12px; }
h2 { font-size: 18px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; padding-bottom: 6px; margin: 16px 0 10px; }
h3 { font-size: 15px; margin: 14px 0 8px; }
p  { margin-bottom: 12px; }
ul, ol { margin-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 14px; }   li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
code { font: 700 12px 'JetBrains Mono'; background: #F9F9F9; border: 1px solid #000; padding: 2px 6px; }
pre  { background: #1E1E1E; color: #D4D4D4; border: 2px solid #000; padding: 12px; overflow-x: auto; font: 12px 'JetBrains Mono'; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
th, td { border: 1.5px solid #000; padding: 8px 12px; text-align: left; }
th { background: #E5E5E5; font-weight: 800; }
blockquote { border-left: 4px solid #FFD740; background: #FFFBEA; padding: 10px 14px; font-weight: 500; }
hr { border: none; border-top: 2px solid #E5E5E5; margin: 20px 0; }
```
Toolbar above it: `padding: 6px 12px; background: #F9F9F9; border: 2px solid #000;` with a mono 12px/700 source note on the left and 32px tool buttons (11px/800, white) on the right.

### Screen-Off and Dim Overlays

Screen off (after inactivity):
```css
position: fixed; inset: 0; background-color: #000000; z-index: 999999;
display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
cursor: pointer; touch-action: manipulation;
/* message */ color: #444444; font: 700 13px 'JetBrains Mono'; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px;
```
The message is written in square brackets, e.g. `[ DISPLAY OFF -- TOUCH TO WAKE ]`. Tap anywhere wakes the display.

Software dimming: a full-screen black div, `pointer-events: none; z-index: 9990;`, whose opacity is driven by the brightness slider.

### System Update Screen (dedicated full-screen window)

- Backdrop: `background-color: #F4F4F0; background-image: radial-gradient(#CFCFC8 1.25px, transparent 1.25px); background-size: 20px 20px;` -- a technical dot grid. This is the only textured backdrop in the system and is reserved for screens that take over the whole device.
- Shell: `width: min(980px, 94vw); max-height: 94vh; background: #FFF; border: 4px solid #000; box-shadow: 10px 10px 0px #000; padding: clamp(18px, 3vh, 36px) clamp(20px, 3.2vw, 42px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: clamp(14px, 2.2vh, 24px);`
- Top row (3px bottom border): an amber mode badge with a blinking 10px black square (`animation: blinkDot 1.1s steps(2, start) infinite`, opacity 1 to 0.2) on the left, an elapsed-time chip (mono, #F9F9F9, 2px border) on the right.
- Hero: spinner + headline `clamp(22px, 3vw, 34px)` + muted sub-line `clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 18px)` / 600.
- Progress card (#F9F9F9, 3px border): phase label + big percentage, hero progress bar, three phase steps.
- 2-column telemetry grid.
- Warning footer: flat callout, centered, 800 uppercase, 3px border.
Sizes use `clamp()` here because this window must survive unknown resolutions.

