## Layout Strategy

### Target Display

A landscape touchscreen tablet (3:2). The app window is created at 1800 x 1200 device pixels multiplied by a configurable resolution factor, and page content is scaled with a configurable zoom factor. Consequently:
- Layouts are fluid in proportion (fr units, flex) but fixed in component size (px).
- `overflow: hidden` on body -- the page never scrolls. Overflow is contained in lists, logs and dialog bodies.
- No breakpoint media queries. Do not build mobile/tablet/desktop variants.
- Always set `min-width: 0` and `min-height: 0` on flex/grid children that contain scrolling or long mono text, or they will blow out the layout.

### Archetype A -- Launcher (centered + 4 corners)

```css
body { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; min-height: 100vh; overflow: hidden; }
.container { max-width: 1440px; width: 100%; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem; }
```
Center: heading, one muted line of instruction (weight 500), then a wrapping centered row of 200 x 70px app buttons (`gap: 20px; margin-top: 30px`). The center card has no border on the launcher.

Fixed corners:
```
Top-Left:     System actions (Shutdown, Reboot, Reload)   fixed; top: 20px; left: 20px;  gap 12px; z 100
Top-Center:   Brightness bar                              fixed; top: 20px; left: 50%; translateX(-50%); z 100
Top-Right:    Help + Wi-Fi buttons                        fixed; top: 20px; right: 20px; gap 12px; z 100
Bottom-Left:  Status + version badges (stacked)           fixed; bottom: 20px; left: 20px;  z 10
Bottom-Right: Connected devices widget                    fixed; bottom: 20px; right: 20px; z 10
```

### Archetype B -- Tool Workstation (work column + sidebar)

```css
.app-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 66fr 34fr;     /* 3fr 1fr when the sidebar holds only a few buttons */
  gap: 12px;
  padding: 10px;
  width: 100vw; height: 100vh;
}
.left-column { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; height: 100%; min-height: 0; min-width: 0; }
```

Work column (left), top to bottom:
1. Control panel card (`flex: 1`): title row (h2 20px + header badges right) -> hero action button -> status readout -> checklist.
2. Log panel card (collapsible).
For scan-driven tools the work column is instead a status headline above two inset screens, with no card border around them.

Sidebar (right, one card or a stack of cards, `gap: 12px`):
1. "SYSTEM CONTROLS" -- sidebar h2, then rows of `.btn-sys` (`display: flex; gap: 12px`, each `flex: 1`).
2. `hr` (2px solid black).
3. "SETTINGS" -- selects, checkboxes, input + inline button, Apply button (primary).
4. Exit button pinned to the bottom with `margin-top: auto` -- Danger-text style, full width.

Catalogue variant: the work column is one large card with a page heading and a scrolling tile grid; the sidebar stacks settings card, a small secondary grid card, log card and exit button.

### Archetype C -- Dialog over scrim
See "Dialogs". Content never scrolls the page; long content scrolls inside the dialog (`max-height: 90vh; overflow-y: auto` on the inner region).

### Archetype D -- Full-screen takeover
Help (white, replaces the viewport), blocking overlay (95% white veil), system update (dot-grid backdrop), screen-off (black).

